# Line endings are not cosmetic here.
#
# The hub SERVES dist/setup.sh to macOS teammates, who run it with bash. A file
# checked out with CRLF on this Windows machine and then uploaded produces
# `$'\r': command not found` on their side — a setup script that fails on the
# first line, for a reason nothing in the error names. That happened on the
# first deploy and had to be fixed with a `sed -i` on the server, which is a
# repair, not a fix.
#
# So: everything textual is LF in the repository and LF in the working tree,
# whatever platform it is checked out on. Node does not care about CRLF, bash
# does, and one rule for both is fewer things to remember.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf

# PowerShell is the one exception: it is only ever run on Windows, and CRLF is
# what every other .ps1 on that machine uses.
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

# Binaries, untouched.
*.woff2 binary
*.png   binary
*.ico   binary
*.exe   binary
